# Normalize text to LF in the repo and the working tree. The plugin is plain
# ESM that the desktop loader and the test harness parse with line-anchored
# regexes; CRLF breaks both.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are executed by /bin/sh (and, for .command, by Finder on
# macOS through its shebang): a CRLF byte after "#!" makes the kernel report
# "bad interpreter" and the script never runs. `text=auto` already lands them
# on LF; these rules state the requirement instead of relying on git's
# binary/text heuristic to keep noticing.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf

# Binary assets are never text. The catalog banner (docs/chroma-banner.png) is
# a PNG: `text=auto` leaves it alone today because git's heuristic sees the
# NUL bytes, but an explicit rule cannot be defeated by a future file whose
# first chunk happens to look like text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
